@nszzj/dsh-android-scrcpy README · dsh-android-scrcpy：**DSH 的安卓投屏 provider** —— 让 DSH 通过 `adb` 连上安卓设备：看画面、点/滑、按键、读控件树、给 AI 看。

> 中文 | **[English](./README.en.md)**

界面、AI 工具、设备与焦点、路由、门槛**全在 core 里**；本包只负责"**这台设备怎么连、怎么点、怎么出画面**"。

@nszzj/dsh-android-scrcpy README · 环境要求：- `adb`（按「连接设置里的路径 → 环境变量 → PATH」依次找）
- 一台安卓设备 + USB 调试（或已配对的无线调试）
- **不需要 Java** —— scrcpy-server 由设备上的 `app_process` 直接跑

@nszzj/dsh-android-scrcpy README · 已知限制：- **连接中途不能改缩放/帧率**：两个平台都不支持中途换档，要换就**断开重连**（改设置只对下次连接生效）
- **首次连接/授权类弹窗**要人在设备上点确认，provider 不能代劳
- 断流/切后台后的恢复依赖 **GOP 补发**；若设备端太久没出关键帧，恢复会慢一点

@nszzj/dsh-android-scrcpy README · dsh-android-scrcpy：**The Android provider for DSH** — connects DSH to Android devices over `adb`: see the screen, tap/scroll, press keys, read the control tree, and let the AI do the same.

All UI, AI tools, device/focus state, routing and permission gates **live in core**; this package only knows **how to talk to this device, how to tap it, and how to produce frames**.

> **[中文](./README.md)** | English

@nszzj/dsh-android-scrcpy README · Install：- Install both, not just the provider (without core this package stays inactive)
- After installing, **fully quit DSH and reopen it** (host-side changes need a restart; client-side only needs a refresh)
- Provider without core: silently inactive because its injection is unsatisfied (by design, not a bug)

@nszzj/dsh-android-scrcpy README · Requirements：- `adb` (looked up via the path in Connection settings → environment → `PATH`)
- An Android device with USB debugging (or paired wireless debugging)
- **No Java needed** — `scrcpy-server` runs through `app_process` on the device

@nszzj/dsh-android-scrcpy README · Known limitations：- **Scale / frame rate cannot change mid-connection**: neither platform supports it; disconnect and reconnect (settings apply to the next connection)
- **First-connection / authorization dialogs** must be confirmed on the device; the provider cannot do it for you
- Recovery after a dropped stream or a backgrounded app relies on **GOP replay**; if the device has not produced a keyframe for a long time, recovery is slower
